A||||41||Cliff Pennock||Posting Images - Beta Testers Needed||||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||09-03-99||11:39 AM||||Ok, I said I was working on a program which allows you to easily post images here. The program is now in Beta Stage and I'm looking for people here that want to beta-test it. You don't need to have your own webspace to post images to, and you can use it for other Forums (on other websites) too.<p>Since I have tested the program only on my machines at the office, I can't guarantee it will not mess up your computer but I really think it's very safe.<p>So if you are interested, just post a message here. I can get your email out of your profile and I will email you instructions on how to download the program and how to use it.<p>Like I said, you don't need your own webspace for posting images, so anybody here can apply for beta-testing.<p>Let me know.
Z||000001||Patrick||09-03-99||12:00 PM||||<br>Ummm....Cliff, just what do you mean by "mess up"? <p>I use my computer for non-linear video editing and I would hate to create an unstable environment. There's no-one at this site who would like to help with this process more than me, but I'm a little leery.<p>Is there anything else you can add that would make me feel a little less apprehensive?<p><p><p>
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||09-03-99||12:10 PM||||well.. if Patrick is using windows, I don't think it can get any more unstable. <IMG SRC="/ubb/wink.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>seriously tho, it sounds like a cool idea. how does it work? What I was thinking you'd set up is an http file upload to some server space provided for people to post images..<br>might be complications there with filenames and stuff, so I'm not sure how well that would work for multiple users uploading files. works ok for one or two people however, as I used something like that during a school project this spring. 
