Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||09-03-99||02:51 PM||||It's a Windows program and the "mess up" part is just a precaution from my side. I've installed the program on several machines now and it's really safe... But it <b>is</b>a Windows program and you really can't trust anything based on a Microsoft product. <IMG SRC="/ubb/wink.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>All I want to see is: please don't hold <b>me</b> responsible if anything goes wrong. If you use the computer you are going to test it on for anything that is of life-importance, don't beta-test it.
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||09-03-99||02:53 PM||||Ah - first time I don't proof-read my post and it's filled with spelling errors...
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||09-04-99||02:20 PM||||Ok, I shouldn't have mentioned the "mess up" bit! <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>What I meant to say was that it really is as save as any other program. But I just want you to realise it's a beta version and you might experience a few bugs here and there that I haven't discovered - nothing really serious. Your machine will not get destroyed, other programs will still work, your files will not be deleted...<p>But my last remark still stands: if you use your machine for something of life-importance, you shouldn't beta test any program on that machine...<p>Let me demonstrate:<p> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero2.jpg"> <p>This took me about 4 mouseclicks to post! (that included uploading the image to the server!).
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||09-04-99||02:25 PM||||DarkLord,<p>The program is very smart and will automatically rename files with duplicate names. You really should see it - it works perfectly.
