Z||000028||Patrick||09-05-99||11:36 AM||||<br>Cliff, you ignored my question!<br>Should I interpret that as meaning "<b>NO</b>"? <IMG SRC="/ubb/frown.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>
Z||000029||Cliff Pennock||09-05-99||11:51 AM||||Sorry Patrick, didn't mean to. Yes I could change the program so it could upload wav's or ani's. But it wasn't meant to become a general upload program. I just noticed how many people were having difficulties posting pictures and thought that was a shame.<p>Anyway, uploading wav's or ani's wouldn't make any sense for this forum since the forum's software can't handle these file types. Remember, I didn't change anything to the forum's software, so PIP should work on <i>any</i> forum. Which reminds me - please don't use the upload area I created for posting images on <b>other</b> forums...
Z||000030||Cliff Pennock||09-05-99||11:53 AM||||88 Fiero: I've sent you an email with the instructions.
Z||000031||Patrick||09-05-99||04:55 PM||||<br>Cliff, the reason why I tried using HTML code a couple of posts back was to see if the <b>forum's</b> software could handle it. I found out that it couldn't, so yes, it's apparent that it's the forum's software which is the limiting factor. <p>I know you've demonstrated in the past that you're able to make changes to the forum's software, so I was just wondering if these kind of changes (to be able to post <b>wav</b> and/or <b>avi</b> files) have ever been considered. True, there wouldn't be a lot of need to be able to post these kind files, but IF it is NOT difficult to change the forum's capabilities, why not? <p>It might be fun to be able to show a short <b>video</b> clip of a Fiero in action (at the strip, etc), or it could be of benefit to be able to hear an <b>audio</b> clip of an odd sound that one of our Fieros is making for diagnostic purposes.<p>Whether these kind of changes are considered by you or not, I'm still happy that you've made it much easier for all of us to post our own pictures at this site.<IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p> 
Z||000032||Cliff Pennock||09-05-99||05:14 PM||||Actually, it's pretty simple to change the forum's software so it supports wav's or ani's but the only problem I have with that is that both file formats tend to give pretty huge files because they're both uncompressed formats... I've only set aside about 300Mb for posting images - that's about 10,000 jpegs or 100 wavs! <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>Perhaps it would be a better idea to support RealAudio/Video files, which actually is already supported, and there's a freeware version for creating RealContent...
Z||000033||Patrick||09-05-99||07:12 PM||||<br>Hey, if there's another option that would work better, that would be great!<p>Cliff, there's no rush for you to set it up. Tomorrow would be fine.<IMG SRC="/ubb/biggrin.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p><p>
